X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: a whole-day event whose end is BEFORE its start covers its start day
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:and nothing else. Only a broken calendar writes this, but the answer used to be three
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:days - the 27th, 28th and 29th of December - because the gap between two days is always
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:counted as a positive number. Two of those three days appear nowhere in the file, and a
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:broken calendar is exactly the situation in which invented dates get believed.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:allday-backwards-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261227
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261224
SUMMARY:End before start
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
